# ==============================================================================
# .env.example - Environment Secrets & Configuration Template
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# DO NOT commit your .env file to Git!
# ==============================================================================

# Automated Secret Generation during ./manage_k8s.sh apps
# gitops/bootstrap/install-argocd.sh and scripts-kubeadm/00_config.sh to automatically check for .env.

# 1. Proxmox Infrastructure Defaults
PROXMOX_IP=192.168.1.35
PROXMOX_USER=root
K8S_USER=ubuntu
K8S_PASSWORD=YourSecurePasswordHere!

# 2. Docker Hub Credentials (for private images / rate limit bypass)
DOCKER_USER=your_dockerhub_username
DOCKER_TOKEN=your_dockerhub_personal_access_token_here
DOCKER_EMAIL=your_email@example.com

# 3. Persistent Storage (SMB / CIFS Share Credentials)
# Share: //192.168.1.29/shared
SMB_USER=smbuser
SMB_PASS=YourSecureSmbPasswordHere

# 4. Optional: Authelia Admin Password
AUTHELIA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=YourAutheliaPasswordHere

## Next Step: Industry-Standard GitOps Secret Management

### Bitnami Sealed Secrets

# - Run `kubeseal < secret.yaml > sealedsecret.yaml`.
# - The output is an asymmetrically encrypted Kubernetes custom resource.
# - Commit `sealedsecret.yaml` safely to GitHub.
# - Only the in-cluster Sealed Secrets Controller can decrypt it and create the corresponding Kubernetes Secret.

### External Secrets Operator (ESO)

# - Connects your cluster to a centralised secret store such as HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, or Doppler.
# - ArgoCD syncs `ExternalSecret` manifests.
# - ESO retrieves the secrets at runtime and automatically creates Kubernetes Secrets for applications.

### Recommendation

# Start with **Bitnami Sealed Secrets** for simple, GitOps-friendly secret management. As the platform matures, adopt **External Secrets Operator (ESO)** with a secret manager such as HashiCorp Vault for an enterprise-grade solution.